Return value of a configuration defined in YAML configuration.

If the value is undefined, empty string is returned. Otherwise return
value, array or JSON object.

To get the complete configuration, use dot as a path, for example:
`zwe config get --config zowe.yaml --path .`

To get subset of configuration or specific value, use comma separated path:

`zwe config get --config zowe.yaml --path zowe.setup`
`zwe config get --config zowe.yaml --path zowe.setup.dataset.prefix`

To get specific item in array, use square brackets. Array starts with index 0.

```yaml
zowe:
  externalDomains:
    - zero.example.com
    - one.example.com
    - two.example.com
```
`zwe config get -c 'PARMLIB(ZOWE.PARMS(YAML))' -p zowe.externalDomains[1]` returns `one.example.com`.
`zwe config get -c 'PARMLIB(ZOWE.PARMS(YAML))' -p zowe.externalDomains[]` returns all items.
`zwe config get -c 'PARMLIB(ZOWE.PARMS(YAML))' -p zowe.externalDomains` returns all items too.
